Against the literal ACs and scope boundaries, the implementation matches AC1–AC7: full roster chips, the exact disabled attributes, toggle/cap behavior, empty-attendance fallback, saved selected+disabled restoration, and both required deletions. Pass 3a adds no new acceptance failure. It does clarify that the selected-and-disabled state I flagged cold is explicitly mandated by AC6, so I’m preserving the original product-risk finding while recording that it is not a spec violation. I’m freezing that conclusion now, before reading the author’s record.
